Trans:
-️**Tips for pedestrians how to remain visible in the dark, when due to energy savings and blackouts, the streets of cities are poorly lit

So:
▪️ Wear light;
Buy reflective elements: bracelet, ribbon on a backpack. Reflectors reduce the risk of hitting a pedestrian by six times;
Buy for your pets glowing collars or clothes with reflective elements.

The most noticeable retro-reflective elements are yellow and larger than 15 cm sq. They should be worn.
From the side of the movement of the car in relation to you, and preferably from both sides;
At the eye level of the driver;
Children are better placed at the level of the head, body and hands;
On the moving parts of the body (forearms, shins, wrists, ankles).

